## Strategy: TRIX(14) Signal-Line Cross

Source citation: Unknown author, Trix Strategy Trading System, forexstrategiesresources.com, 2013. URL: local PDF archive.

Target symbols: EURUSD.DWX, GBPUSD.DWX, USDJPY.DWX, AUDUSD.DWX. Period: H1.
Expected trades per year per symbol: 30, based on H1 oscillator signal-line crosses.

TRIX is a triple-smoothed EMA-based momentum oscillator. Signal: cross of TRIX over its own signal line.

### TRIX Calculation

1. EMA(14) of close
2. EMA(14) of step 1
3. EMA(14) of step 2 → triple smoothed
4. TRIX = (triple\_smooth\_today / triple\_smooth\_yesterday − 1) × 100
5. Signal line = EMA(9) of TRIX

### Entry Conditions

- **Long**: TRIX crosses above signal line → buy at market on bar close
- **Short**: TRIX crosses below signal line → sell at market on bar close

### Exit

- **SL**: 2×ATR(14) from entry
- **TP**: 4×ATR(14) from entry (R:R = 2.0)
- Alternative exit: reverse TRIX/signal cross (whichever comes first)

### Notes

TRIX is trend-following and lagging due to triple smoothing — it suppresses short-term noise but will be slow at trend turns. Works best in sustained trending markets; generates many false signals in sideways conditions.
